{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789226839,"nonce":"6wJBcIrcN1Vv12+58D93t+Lg+wc=","title":"Python builtins on a typed receiver as BuiltinClass transforms","message":"The natives in crates/zyntax_python/src/runtime.rs take a boxed value\nand read its tag. That is the right shape when the receiver's type is\nunknown at compile time and for print/str, which allocate or do I/O.\nFor a receiver the SSA builder does know, it is a box, a call and a\ntag switch where one instruction would do.\n\nPlan: the frontend rewrites the free-function builtins into method\ncalls on the receiver (`len(s)` to `s.__len__()`, `int(x)` to\n`x.__int__()`, and so on), and zyntax_python registers BuiltinClass\nimplementations through TieredRuntime::register_builtin_class:\n\n- PyNumber, matching int/float/bool: `__int__` is FpToSi or ZExt or\n  the identity, `__float__` SiToFp, `__bool__` a compare with zero,\n  `__abs__` Fabs or a select, `__neg__`, and later `__str__` through\n  the runtime.\n- PyStr, matching the String primitive: `__len__` loads the ZRTL length\n  word (byte length; a code-point count needs the runtime and is the\n  slow path), `upper`/`lower`/`find`/`split`/`join`/`strip` as runtime\n  symbols until a string layout in the IR exists.\n- A receiver typed Unknown falls through to the natives.\n\nThis is also where the language's truthiness lives once the frontend\ncarries a type for names: `not x`, `if x:`, `x or y` on a string or\nnumber become the right compare at HIR level instead of a runtime\n`$Py$bool`.\n\nDepends on the frontend recording a type for names it can know\n(literal initializers, annotated parameters, annotated call returns),\nwhich is the same pass the `and`/`or` value semantics need.","files":null}]}